{"title":"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2.5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2.5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An unfair coin lands on heads with a probability of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/4/c84a414e9655bf25b41aebc8c9f7bcb651acf2fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"9\" height=\"21\" />. When tossed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> times, the probability of exactly two heads is the same as the probability of exactly three heads. What is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74fc23bda9af8b1480f23e8d4dafc8674d4ca02a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\; 5 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\; 8 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\; 10 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\; 11 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\; 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"373\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>When tossed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> times, the probability of getting exactly 2 heads and the rest tails is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc6405c602dee5d12cb017541fb674a4f3bbb8e8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dbinom{n}{2} {\\left( \\frac{1}{4} \\right)}^2 {\\left( \\frac{3}{4} \\right) }^{n-2}.\\]\" width=\"150\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Similarly, the probability of getting exactly 3 heads is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/c/92c95422814935e2a1744e40bb8ff525c4db41a3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dbinom{n}{3}{\\left( \\frac{1}{4} \\right)}^3 {\\left( \\frac{3}{4} \\right) }^{n-3}.\\]\" width=\"150\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Now set the two probabilities equal to each other and solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/e/deed9cb1861f787abde4c577294d240a24de5890.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dbinom{n}{2}{\\left( \\frac{1}{4} \\right)}^2 {\\left( \\frac{3}{4} \\right) }^{n-2}=\\dbinom{n}{3}{\\left( \\frac{1}{4} \\right)}^3 {\\left( \\frac{3}{4} \\right) }^{n-3}\\]\" width=\"320\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/f/07f1b2a26ad277631bd46c1314db7092bcd944c6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{n(n-1)}{2!} \\cdot \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{n(n-1)(n-2)}{3!}  \\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\]\" width=\"272\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/4/5d414de3ecbe06f23e64517629c32e1a0023e6d3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3 = \\frac{n-2}{3}\\]\" width=\"77\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/d/1cd6ebfe15d5b338b44028394dc9b9543fe488f7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n-2 = 9\\]\" width=\"74\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/7/c27f5da250dd157f54a2a7e3c2e4eb2eb7e4ed48.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n = \\fbox{\\textbf{(D)}\\; 11}\\]\" width=\"102\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p><br />\nNote: the original problem did not specify <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/65262bf247c4a3c6114a8223d249dc9702619d3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d96ecc15129c5631ba4a2c6578e91e3d13e3baf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> was a solution, but this was fixed in the Wiki problem text so that the answer would make sense. <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Adihaya\" title=\"User:Adihaya\">— @adihaya</a> (<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User_talk:Adihaya\" title=\"User talk:Adihaya\">talk</a>) 15:23, 19 February 2016 (EST)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Bash it out with the answer choices! (not really a rigorous solution)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2.5\">Solution 2.5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2.5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In order to test the answer choices efficiently, realize that the probability <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> flips yielding two heads is of the form:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/7/e57badeeab7becbe678e1f6ad2c296667e1d2529.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dbinom{n}{2}{\\left(\\frac{1}{4} \\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{3}{4} \\cdot \\frac{3}{4} \\cdot \\frac{3}{4} \\ldots \\right)} = \\dbinom{n}{2}{\\left(\\frac{3^{n-2}}{4^n}\\right)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"345\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Similarly, the form for the probability of three heads is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/c/c8ca0831d7944482c2537575a113ce88ee8c628e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dbinom{n}{3}{\\left(\\frac{3^{n-3}}{4^n}\\right)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"100\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>The probability of getting three heads (comapred to the probability of getting two) from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> flips is missing a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in the numerator. Thus, we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/3/a437de5bd6a33f09d120fb93f3ac1b82a8d1d816.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dbinom{n}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"41\" height=\"55\" /> to add a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to the numerator of the probability of getting three heads.\nOur testing equation becomes\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/4/514dbaae76ec78e6d85fbe7314205aa254e62f61.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dbinom{n}{2} \\times 3 = \\dbinom{n}{3}\\]\" width=\"125\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>since after factoring out the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/3/a437de5bd6a33f09d120fb93f3ac1b82a8d1d816.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dbinom{n}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"41\" height=\"55\" />, the remaining factorizations should be equal. \n</p><p>The only answer choice satisfying this condition is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/9/e69d72d953cec5d6a759b9a16540394c9c38e263.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{\\textbf{(D)}\\;11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"62\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>-Solution by Joeya\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B\">2015 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018000000\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.038 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.062 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 232/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5176/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   15.485      1 -total\n 53.33%    8.259      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 44.68%    6.919      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-